.TH zwwin "" "Command"
.SH NAME
zwwin \- dock widget: running-program count
.SH SYNOPSIS
started by \fBzdock\fR (catalog line \fB@Programs:/usr/hr/bin/zwwin:*\fR)
.SH DESCRIPTION
.HS
zwwin -- dock widget: running-program count
Started by zdock from an @ line of /usr/hr/etc/dock; not run by hand.
Shows how many programs are on the desktop; click for "Switch to...".
.HE
.B zwwin
is a widget of the
.B zdock
bar: a small resident program the dock starts from an
.B @
line of its catalog, showing how many programs are on the desktop
(distinct window-owning clients \- an application with two windows
counts once, and the dock bar itself not at all) in an icon-sized cell
at the right end of the bar.
The count comes from the server-published window list, the same list
.B zmon
shows a column of, and follows the desktop within a second.
.PP
It draws inside the dock's own window under the dock's clipping, owns
no window of its own, and takes no input itself; a left click on the
cell is the dock's, and the shipped catalog wires it (the
.B *
click verb) to the server's
.B "Switch to..."
dialog \- the same window list the desktop menu offers.
It exits by itself when the dock goes away.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.B zdock ,
.B zview ,
.B zmon
.SH NOTES
Not meant to be run from a shell: it needs the cell contract
.RB ( \-W )
that only
.B zdock
supplies, and exits at once without it.
Minimised (hidden) windows still belong to running programs and are
counted.
